    "Consider the economic implications of absolute scarcity in an era of infinite fiat currency printing. Gold is scarce, but when the price of gold doubles, mining corporations deploy capital to explore new deposits, expanding annual gold production. Bitcoin's supply, by contrast, is completely inelastic: regardless of whether the price of Bitcoin is one thousand dollars or one million dollars, the programmatic emission rate cannot be increased.",
