    "Limit your digital asset exposure strictly to the dominant blue-chip protocols (Bitcoin and, to a lesser extent, Ethereum). Refuse to gamble your hard-earned savings on trending social media tokens, decentralized finance (DeFi) yield farms, or anonymous Discord trading groups. Treat digital assets as long-term monetary stores of value, not lottery tickets.",
    "If you choose to hold actual native cryptocurrency rather than institutional ETFs, you must master Self-Custody and Cold Storage Security. Centralized crypto exchanges?such as Coinbase, Kraken, or Binance?are private commercial entities. When you leave your assets on an exchange, you do not own the underlying keys; you own an IOU.",
